From d78dd7ccf9346dd4ddaa2576f4e40f025e6ff97f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 19 Jun 2026 08:43:32 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02785/11362] [outer-loop] #2 ARC artifact-discipline helper:
 emit honest inference_substrate, plug the gate leak

The .409/.410 leak: real transfer-solves (e.g. .410 exp4433 -- ka59's win-rule -> g50t L1, +1 level,
offline_reproduced) ran <1s deterministic and declared NO inference_substrate, so adversarial_verify
applied the strict 60s live-model floor and DURATION_TOO_SHORT-quarantined a REAL win. Root cause:
declaring inference_substrate at the TASK level is not enough -- the agent must EMIT it in the artifact.
This canonical, non-gate-weakening helper computes the honest substrate from what the run actually did
(live LLM call -> 60s floor; deterministic reproduction/transfer -> 100us floor; cached-candidate
scoring -> 1s floor) and lints an artifact for a present+plausible bare declaration. Demonstrated
catching the real g50t artifact (flags the miss, computes aggregation_from_upstream_artifacts as the
honest value). Isolated new module (no conflict with the conductor's concurrent arc_solver_kit edits);
exp4437's lint + the .411 ARC tasks reference REQUIRED_SUBSTRATE_PRINCIPLE. 8 tests pass; does NOT relax
the fabrication gate (a real model run still claims live_llm_inference).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
